#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Copyright 2026 Theorem Labs, PBC
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""The verdict of an enrollment's review, as the check run `Enrollment review` of the oss-verify App records it:

    VERDICTS=<json> REASONS=<json> HEAD_SHA=<commit> [CRITICALITY_SCORE=<number>] [OSS_FUZZ=true|false] \\
      [SIZES=<json>] .github/scripts/review-verdict
    HOLD=screen|cap|failed [FREE=<time>] [JOB=gather|screen|review|hold] RUN_URL=<run> REPO=<owner/repo> \\
      PR=<number> HEAD_SHA=<commit> [CRITICALITY_SCORE=<number>] [OSS_FUZZ=true|false] [SIZES=<json>] \\
      .github/scripts/review-verdict
    .github/scripts/review-verdict --ids
    .github/scripts/review-verdict --sentence success|failure|action_required

build.yaml's comment job runs it in its step "Post the comment and record the verdict", which posts the check run
from what it prints: one JSON object with `conclusion`, `title`, `summary` and `text`. The step posts `text` as the
check run's `output.text`, the record (below).

VERDICTS is the review's structured output `verdicts`, the id of each check of review.md to `pass`, `fail`, `person`
or, for F5 and F8 alone, `optional`; REASONS is its `reasons`, an id to the sentences that decide the verdict. An id
that VERDICTS does not give, or gives another value, counts as `person`, with the reason "the review gave no verdict".
The conclusion is `failure` when one check is `fail`, `success` when every check is `pass` or `optional`, and
`action_required` otherwise. The summary lists each check that is not `pass`, worst first, with its reason. A reason is
what a pull request can steer, so each goes through .github/scripts/review-neutralize --drop-markers, as the comment's
text does, and the summary stays under the 65,535 characters GitHub takes.

HOLD gives no verdict of the review: the screen held the pull request, the daily cap stopped it (FREE, route's output
free, the time the cap lets it run), or a job of the run failed (JOB). Each is `action_required`, with fixed words.

The record is the review as programs read it (dispatch://OSSV-275's Enrollment view, dispatch://OSSV-623's hold
counts): one JSON object in an HTML comment, which GitHub does not show. Each record has all of these keys, in this
order:

    schema             "oss-verify/enrollment-review/1".
    head               HEAD_SHA, the commit of the check run. It must be 40 lower-case hexadecimal digits: else this
                       stops with exit status 2 and prints nothing.
    hold               HOLD: "screen", "cap" or "failed". It is null when the review gave verdicts.
    job                JOB ("gather", "screen", "review" or "hold") when hold is "failed", else null.
    verdicts           For a review, each id of IDS, in that order, to the verdict that the summary counts: an id
                       that VERDICTS does not give, or gives another value, is "person". For a hold, {}.
    criticality_score  CRITICALITY_SCORE, the criticality score that .github/scripts/triage.py computed, to 5 places
                       (its table shows 2).
    oss_fuzz           OSS_FUZZ: true when one of the OSS-Fuzz projects that triage.py reads (the OSS_FUZZ_CANDIDATES
                       projects whose names are most like the repository's) has this repository as its main_repo,
                       false when none of them has.
    sizes              SIZES, the object of .github/scripts/binary-sizes as it is (the project-builds job's output
                       sizes): {target: {build: {"text": ..., "exec": ...}}}.

criticality_score and oss_fuzz are null when they are not known: the repository is a fork (for criticality_score
only: a fork is not scored), it is not on github.com or GitHub does not find it, its row could not be checked, or the
run had no gather (the daily cap) or its gather failed before the triage. A gather that fails after the triage, at the
fetch of the source, can still give the two values: they are then the values that the run got. Only a JSON number
that is finite and not a boolean is a CRITICALITY_SCORE, only the text true or false is an OSS_FUZZ, and only a JSON
object is a SIZES. Any other value is null, and so is a value that is not given.

The text is json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(",", ":")), with each "<", ">" and "&" replaced by
\\u003c, \\u003e and \\u0026, in "<!-- " and " -->". A JSON parser reads each escape back as the same character. The
escapes are necessary, in keys too: GitHub shows output.text as Markdown, and a target is a file name that the pull
request's build chooses. Measured 2026-11-17 with GitHub's POST /markdown (gfm), the first line below shows nothing,
but the second shows <b>shown</b> and a link to the account it mentions:

    <!-- {"a\\u003e--\\u003e @octocat #12":...} -->
    <!-- {"x":"a --> <b>shown</b> @octocat"} -->

The text has at most 65,535 characters, GitHub's limit for output.text. When it would be longer, sizes keeps only the
"plain" build of each target (a target whose value is not an object, or has no "plain" build, keeps {}). When it is
still longer, sizes is null, and one line on standard error says why. Standard output stays one JSON object.

A reader takes the newest check run Enrollment review of the oss-verify App (id 5447700) whose external_id is the
pull request's number, as .github/scripts/enroll-dispatch does. It removes the first 5 and the last 4 characters of
its output.text and parses the JSON. It ignores each key that it does not know: dispatch://OSSV-661 writes records of
the same schema from another repository, with keys of its own. A check run from before the record has output.text
null, and so no record.

--ids prints each check id of review.md, in its order, with the verdicts it takes, as one JSON object: the one list,
which .github/scripts/review-prompt puts in the review's schema. --sentence prints the first sentence of the review
comment for a conclusion, which .github/scripts/review-body writes."""
import datetime
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import math
import os
import pathlib
import re
import sys

# Every check of review.md's checklist, in its order: a numbered item of a section is the section's letter and its
# number, and a section with no numbered item is its letter alone.
IDS = ["A1", "A2", "A3", "A4", "A5", "A6", "B", "C1", "C2", "C3", "C4", "C5", "C6", "C7", "D1", "D2", "D3", "E",
       "F1", "F2", "F3", "F4", "F5", "F6", "F7", "F8", "G1", "G2", "G3", "G4", "G5"]
# The verdicts each check takes: a weak fail of F5 or F8 is optional (review.md, "Verdicts").
TAKES = {check: ["pass", "fail", "person"] + (["optional"] if check in ("F5", "F8") else []) for check in IDS}
# The worst first: the order of the summary.
ORDER = ("fail", "person", "optional")
SENTENCES = {
    "success": "No change is needed.",
    "failure": "The changes below are needed.",
    "action_required": "No change is asked of you, and the review left some checks open.",
}
JOBS = ("gather", "screen", "review", "hold")
NO_VERDICT = "The review gave no verdict."
NO_REASON = "The review gave no reason."
# A reason's length, after review-neutralize: 31 reasons of REASON_LIMIT keep the summary under the 65,535 characters
# GitHub takes.
REASON_LIMIT = 1500
# The record's schema.
SCHEMA = "oss-verify/enrollment-review/1"
# GitHub's limit for a check run's output.text, in characters.
TEXT_LIMIT = 65535
# The escape of each character that can end the record's HTML comment, or start a tag or a character reference.
ESCAPES = {ord("<"): "\\u003c", ord(">"): "\\u003e", ord("&"): "\\u0026"}

# No bytecode file beside the scripts: the job's checkout is main's, and only read.
sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
_loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(
    "review_neutralize", str(pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().with_name("review-neutralize")))
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("review_neutralize", _loader)
neutralize = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
_loader.exec_module(neutralize)


def die(message):
    print(f"review-verdict: {message}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)


def as_object(text):
    """A JSON object, or {} for anything else: a value the review did not give decides nothing."""
    try:
        value = json.loads(text or "")
    except ValueError:
        return {}
    return value if isinstance(value, dict) else {}


def parsed(text):
    """The JSON value of text, or None when text is not JSON."""
    try:
        return json.loads(text or "")
    except (ValueError, RecursionError):
        return None


def head():
    """HEAD_SHA, the commit of the check run."""
    sha = os.environ.get("HEAD_SHA", "")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", sha):
        die("HEAD_SHA is not a commit of 40 lower-case hexadecimal digits")
    return sha


def score(text):
    """CRITICALITY_SCORE as a number, or None when it is not a finite JSON number."""
    value = parsed(text)
    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, (int, float)):
        return None
    # An int is always finite, and math.isfinite() cannot take one that is too large for a float.
    return value if isinstance(value, int) or math.isfinite(value) else None


def reason(text):
    """A reason as the summary shows it: neutralized as the comment's text is, on one line, cut at REASON_LIMIT."""
    if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.strip():
        return NO_REASON
    return " ".join(neutralize.neutralize(text, True).split())[:REASON_LIMIT] or NO_REASON


def from_verdicts(verdicts, reasons):
    """The conclusion, title and summary of a review, and the verdict that it counts for each check."""
    found, counted = {}, {}
    for check in IDS:
        verdict = verdicts.get(check)
        if verdict not in TAKES[check]:
            verdict = "person"
            found[check] = (verdict, NO_VERDICT)
        elif verdict != "pass":
            found[check] = (verdict, reason(reasons.get(check)))
        counted[check] = verdict
    kinds = {verdict for verdict, _ in found.values()}
    conclusion = "failure" if "fail" in kinds else "action_required" if "person" in kinds else "success"
    sentence = SENTENCES[conclusion]
    lines = [f"- **{check}** ({verdict}): {text}"
             for kind in ORDER for check, (verdict, text) in found.items() if verdict == kind]
    summary = sentence + ("\n\n" + "\n".join(lines) if lines else "")
    return conclusion, sentence, summary, counted


def from_hold(hold):
    """The conclusion, title and summary of a hold, and the job that failed (None for a hold that is not failed)."""
    repo, pr = os.environ.get("REPO", ""), os.environ.get("PR", "")
    run_url = os.environ.get("RUN_URL", "")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+", repo):
        die("REPO is not owner/repository")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[1-9][0-9]*", pr):
        die("PR is not a number")
    run = re.fullmatch(r"https://[A-Za-z0-9.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/actions/runs/([0-9]+)", run_url)
    if not run:
        die("RUN_URL is not the address of a run")
    job = None
    if hold == "screen":
        title = "The automated screen held this pull request."
        summary = (f"{title} It comes from, or holds the text of, an account without write access to this repository,"
                   " so an automated screen reads it before the automated review does, and the screen did not pass it"
                   " or could not read it. No review ran. Theorem decides the next step.")
    elif hold == "cap":
        cap, author = os.environ.get("REVIEW_CAP", ""), os.environ.get("REVIEW_CAP_AUTHOR", "")
        if not (cap.isdigit() and author.isdigit()):
            die("REVIEW_CAP and REVIEW_CAP_AUTHOR are not numbers")
        try:
            free = datetime.datetime.strptime(os.environ.get("FREE", ""), "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
        except ValueError:
            die("FREE is not a time such as 2026-11-09T12:00:00Z")
        title = "The daily cap of automated reviews held this pull request."
        summary = (f"{title} It comes from an account without write access to this repository, and the automated"
                   f" reviews of such accounts reached their cap of {cap} in 24 hours, {author} for one author. From"
                   f" {free:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M} UTC, a push or `gh workflow run build.yaml -R {repo} -f pr={pr}` reviews"
                   " it.")
    elif hold == "failed":
        job = os.environ.get("JOB", "")
        if job not in JOBS:
            die(f"JOB is not one of {', '.join(JOBS)}")
        title = f"The {job} job failed."
        summary = (f"The {job} job of [this run]({run_url}) failed, so the review gave no verdict."
                   f" `gh run rerun {run.group(1)} --failed -R {repo}` reviews it.")
    else:
        die("HOLD is not screen, cap or failed")
    return "action_required", title, summary, job


def as_text(record):
    """The record as output.text: its JSON in an HTML comment, with no character that can end that comment."""
    return "<!-- " + json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(",", ":")).translate(ESCAPES) + " -->"


def fitted(record):
    """The record's text, at most TEXT_LIMIT characters: with only the plain build of each target when the sizes of
    all builds make it longer, and with sizes null when it is still longer."""
    text = as_text(record)
    if len(text) <= TEXT_LIMIT:
        return text
    # Only sizes can make the text so long: each other value is short.
    plain = {target: {"plain": builds["plain"]} if isinstance(builds, dict) and "plain" in builds else {}
             for target, builds in record["sizes"].items()}
    text = as_text({**record, "sizes": plain})
    if len(text) <= TEXT_LIMIT:
        return text
    print(f"review-verdict: the record's text is over {TEXT_LIMIT:,} characters with only the plain builds of SIZES,"
          " so its sizes is null", file=sys.stderr)
    return as_text({**record, "sizes": None})


def main():
    arguments = sys.argv[1:]
    if arguments == ["--ids"]:
        print(json.dumps(TAKES))
        return
    if len(arguments) == 2 and arguments[0] == "--sentence":
        if arguments[1] not in SENTENCES:
            die("the conclusion is not success, failure or action_required")
        print(SENTENCES[arguments[1]])
        return
    if arguments:
        die("usage: review-verdict [--ids | --sentence CONCLUSION]")
    sha = head()
    hold = os.environ.get("HOLD", "")
    if hold:
        conclusion, title, summary, job = from_hold(hold)
        verdicts = {}
    else:
        conclusion, title, summary, verdicts = from_verdicts(as_object(os.environ.get("VERDICTS")),
                                                             as_object(os.environ.get("REASONS")))
        job = None
    sizes = parsed(os.environ.get("SIZES"))
    record = {"schema": SCHEMA, "head": sha, "hold": hold or None, "job": job, "verdicts": verdicts,
              "criticality_score": score(os.environ.get("CRITICALITY_SCORE")),
              "oss_fuzz": {"true": True, "false": False}.get(os.environ.get("OSS_FUZZ")),
              "sizes": sizes if isinstance(sizes, dict) else None}
    print(json.dumps({"conclusion": conclusion, "title": title, "summary": summary, "text": fitted(record)}))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
